# Pin working-tree line endings to LF so the checked-out bytes are identical to
# the stored bytes. The repo is configured with `core.autocrlf=true`; without a
# pinned attribute git reports a `stat()` size for a modified file that differs
# from the file actually on disk (it will normalize to CRLF "next time it
# touches" the file). That mismatch trips byte-for-byte tooling that stats a
# file before and after reading it — most visibly the secret-scan snapshot in
# autoreview, which aborts on "file changed while reading".
#
# The stored blobs are already LF, so this changes no content; it only makes
# the working copy byte-identical to the blob from the start.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending-converted.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.eot  binary
